.TH CURLDBG 1 "June 2026" "curldbg" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
curldbg \- lightweight HTTP/HTTPS client and request debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B curldbg
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIurl\fR
.P
.B curldbg
\-\-compare [\fIoptions\fR] \fIurl\fR
.P
.B curldbg
\-\-compare-urls [\fIoptions\fR] \fIurl-a\fR \fIurl-b\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B curldbg
performs a single HTTP/HTTPS request (GET/POST/PUT/HEAD), reports per-hop timing
metrics (DNS, TCP connect, TTFB, total), and prints a short preview of the response
body. It can follow redirects, track the full redirect chain with per-hop timing,
compare IPv4 vs IPv6, or compare two URLs side-by-side.
.P
When stdout is not a TTY, curldbg auto-silences normal output and writes the raw
response body to stdout (pipe-friendly). If no URL scheme is given, https:// is
assumed.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Request control"
.TP
.B \-X, \-\-request \fIGET|POST|PUT|HEAD\fR
Choose HTTP method (default: GET).
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-data \fIbody\fR
Send request body. Defaults method to POST if \-X is not set.
Prefix with @ to read from a file (\fB@file\fR) or stdin (\fB@\-\fR).
Repeatable \(em values are concatenated with &.
.TP
.B \-\-data-binary
Alias for \-d.
.TP
.B \-T, \-\-upload-file \fIfile\fR
Upload file as the PUT request body (single request mode only).
.TP
.B \-I, \-\-head
Perform a HEAD request (headers only, no body).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fail
Exit with non-zero status on HTTP status >= 400.
.SS "Output control"
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-silent
Suppress normal timing/output display.
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-show-error
Show error messages even when \-s is active.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print request headers (> prefix) and response headers (< prefix) to stderr.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIfile\fR
Write response body to file (single request mode only).
.TP
.B \-O, \-\-remote-name
Write response body using the URL's filename component (single request mode only).
.TP
.B \-\-progress-bar
Accepted for curl compatibility (no-op).
.SS "TLS / Auth"
.TP
.B \-k, \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-user \fIuser:pass\fR
Use HTTP Basic authentication.
.TP
.B -A, \-\-user-agent \fIstring\fR
Set a custom User-Agent header (default: curldbg/1.0).
.SS "Headers"
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-header \fIheader\fR
Add a request header (repeatable). Providing Content-Type, Content-Length, or
Host via \-H skips auto-generation of those headers.
.SS "Connectivity"
.TP
.B \-4
Force IPv4 DNS resolution and connect.
.TP
.B \-6
Force IPv6 DNS resolution and connect.
.TP
.B \-\-no-happy-eyeballs
Disable Happy Eyeballs; connect sequentially (IPv6 then IPv4).
.TP
.B \-\-connect-timeout \fIms\fR
Timeout per connect attempt in milliseconds.
.TP
.B \-\-read-timeout \fIms\fR
Timeout for read/write operations in milliseconds.
.TP
.B \-\-max-time \fIms\fR
Total operation timeout in milliseconds (applied across all phases including
redirects).
.SS "Redirects"
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-location
Follow redirects.
.TP
.B \-\-max-redirs \fIn\fR
Maximum number of redirects when \-L is active (default: 10).
.SS "Compare modes"
.TP
.B \-\-compare
Run the same URL over IPv4 and IPv6 concurrently and print side-by-side metrics
with deltas.
.TP
.B \-\-compare-urls
Run two different URLs concurrently and print side-by-side metrics with deltas.
.SS "Miscellaneous"
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and author.
.SH "OUTPUT FIELDS"
When not in silent mode, curldbg prints:
.TP
.B dns
DNS resolution time in ms.
.TP
.B tcp
TCP connect time in ms.
.TP
.B ttfb
Time to first byte of the response in ms.
.TP
.B total
Total request time in ms.
.TP
.B connected
Connected IP address and address family (IPv4/IPv6).
.TP
.B final url
The final URL after any redirects.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B curldbg https://example.com
Basic GET request with timing output.
.TP
.B curldbg \-L https://httpbin.org/redirect/3
Follow redirects and show the full chain with per-hop timing.
.TP
.B curldbg \-u user:pass \-H "Accept: application/json" https://example.com
Basic auth with a custom Accept header.
.TP
.B curldbg \-X POST \-H "Content-Type: application/json" \-d '{"key":"value"}' https://api.example.com
JSON POST request.
.TP
.B curldbg \-d @data.json https://api.example.com
POST JSON from a file.
.TP
.B curldbg -sS -I https://example.com
Silent HEAD request (check headers only).
.TP
.B curldbg \-\-compare https://example.com
Compare IPv4 vs IPv6 performance.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IP 0
Success.
.IP 1
Generic error (DNS failure, connection refused, TLS error, timeout, etc.).
.SH AUTHOR
Pau Santana.
